  "problem": "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2(x-1)?$",
  "worked_solution": "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int (x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int (x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x-1)^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/92a2dbaa5726e6a1ab83fa879ad7b630b05e68a8e366db214b74d85269a849a9.png)",
